    "text": "Car <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> overtakes another car <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> at a relative speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. How fast will the image of car <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> appear to move in the mirror of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> fitted in car <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, when the car <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> away from the car <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>?",
